/ Mul accepts N,M in decimal 0..32767.
/ Mul writes Product, returning -1 there on invalid input/overflow.
ORG 100
Input
Store N
Input
Store M
JnS Mul
Load Product
Output
Halt
Mul, HEX 0
Load N
Skipcond 000
Jump CheckM
Jump Failure
CheckM, Load M
Skipcond 000
Jump Choose
Jump Failure
Choose, Load N
Subt M
Skipcond 000
Jump NAtLeastM
Jump NLessM
NAtLeastM, Load N
Store Big
Load M
Store Count
Jump Init
NLessM, Load M
Store Big
Load N
Store Count
Init, Clear
Store Product
LoopCheck, Load Count
Skipcond 400
Jump CheckAdd
Jump Return
CheckAdd, Load MaxValue
Subt Product
Subt Big
Skipcond 000
Jump AddSafe
Jump Failure
AddSafe, Load Product
Add Big
Store Product
Load Count
Subt One
Store Count
Jump LoopCheck
Failure, Load NegOne
Store Product
Return, JumpI Mul
N, DEC 0
M, DEC 0
Big, DEC 0
Count, DEC 0
Product, DEC 0
One, DEC 1
MaxValue, DEC 32767
NegOne, DEC -1
END
